<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Kuwohi Observation Tower Trail — Kuwohi Observation Tower Trail</name><desc>The Kuwohi Observation Tower Trail climbs from the summit parking area in Great Smoky Mountains National Park to a concrete spiral ramp above the trees. Clear weather reveals layers of forested mountains in every direction. The full mapped return walk, including the tower ramp, is about 2.1 km. The path is paved but steep enough to require breaks. Fog can hide the main view, and busy periods bring limited parking.

